WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.049
Judge Judith Sheindlin, known to most as Judge
Judy, made a name for herself with her no-nonsense

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:12.170
attitude, tough talk, and long, belittling
lectures she gives to people who appear before

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.529
her. But there are some other details about
this legal lady and her show that she doesn't

00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:19.500
talk about all that much. Since she's too
modest to reveal them herself, we've compiled

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.730
them here for your viewing pleasure.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.590
Ambulance chasers

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.360
The defendants and plaintiffs who appear before
Judge Judy are neither assigned to her, nor

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.110
do they seek her out. All of that is handled
by the honorable judge's producers. According

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.440
to a letter obtained by Radar Online, the
producers headhunt through small claims courts

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.800
for cases that'd be fun for the rest of the
country to watch on television. In the letter,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.280
producer Julie Turner entices a defendant
into bringing his or her case to Judge Judy

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.039
with the promise of appearing on television,
because let's face it there's no better place

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:50.670
to have a personal matter settled.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.280
Producers pay the fines

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.850
Even though the show claims all of the decisions
are legally binding, they really aren't. That's

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.260
because the fines Judy doles out aren't paid
by the cases' losers, as would happen in real-life

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.049
court cases. They're actually paid by producers.
In the same letter inviting the unknown defendant

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:10.039
to appear on the show, Turner promises that
even if this anonymous person loses the case,

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:14.869
he or she won't be responsible for any fees
or penalties. Any money comes from the producers,

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:18.100
which is a sweet deal for most of the people
who appear on the show, as they tend to have

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.649
little money. If only real court cases worked
this way! And that's not the only money to

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.780
switch hands on behalf of the good judge...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.680
Everyone gets paid

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.229
While it may not be as profitable as hitting
the Powerball, appearing on Judge Judy is

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.520
a financial win-win situation for both the
plaintiffs and the defendants. If anything,

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.109
it's probably the closest thing to an all-expenses-paid
vacation that some of them will ever see.

00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:43.729
Turner's letter goes on to say that in addition
to paying for the case's outcome, the show

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:47.670
also pays appearance fees to all litigants
who appear on the program, along with travel

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.210
expenses for them and any witnesses they wish
to bring along. Of course, those witnesses

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.679
have to have something to do with the case,
but still, a free trip to Los Angeles will

00:01:54.679 --> 00:01:59.899
entice anyone to say anything, which often
leads to Judge Judy's next little known fact.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:01.170
Fake cases?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.960
Obviously, learning that parts, if not all,
of a reality show are staged isn't much of

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.729
a surprise these days. But the makers of Judge
Judy can deny responsibility for some of the

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:14.670
fakery...because some of the people who appear
on the show simply fabricate entire cases

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:19.390
for them. Back in 2010, Vice reported that
Jonathan Coward and his friends Brian and

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.800
Kate concocted an insane story involving two
broken televisions and a dead cat in order

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.060
to get on the show. Coward got the idea from
another friend who appeared on the show in

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.670
the '90s, with an actual case. Producers took
the bait and flew Coward and his three friends

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.050
out. After the taping, the trio celebrated
by renting a convertible and drinking champagne

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.650
in a hot tub for the rest of the day. How
did it feel to take advantage of Judge Judy?

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:44.580
When asked, Coward said, "It felt awesome!
It felt so good." And no, he shouldn't feel

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.850
bad, because...

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.510
She's not a judge

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:52.160
Though Judith Sheindlin was appointed a judge
by Mayor Ed Koch in 1982, she does not preside

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:57.100
as a real judge on television. The set has
all the accessories and details of a courtroom,

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.240
but what Judge Judy does at most is arbitration.
As reported by Consumerist, Judge Judy, and

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.750
other television courts, operate under a contract
of adhesion, meaning they "are not bound by

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.310
real rules of procedure, evidence, or even
behavior." So on her show, Judge Judy isn't

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:15.490
a judge making a legal decision. She's more
of a mediator trying to solve other people's

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.070
problems. So at most, she's just a glorified
middle school vice principal.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.160
She might've taken down a school

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.580
When Tony Robb's mother sent him to Cornerstone
Christian School in Clearlake, CA, she didn't

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.620
think her son would get locked in a storage
closet for hours a day, but that's what happened.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.390
They later appeared before Judge Judy, hoping
she could get them their tuition money back.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:38.900
They never could have predicted what followed.
The defendants' testimony revealed that the

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.340
majority of the staff not only lacked the
necessary skills to deal with special-needs

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.380
students like Tony, but they even lacked Bachelor's
degrees. The principal only held an Associate's

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.750
degree. In case you're not informed about
the requirements of a school administrator,

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:55.340
they go far beyond attending a two-year school.
Even worse: the superintendent only had a

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.920
high school diploma. Following a justifiable
tirade, Sheindlin awarded Tony and his mother

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.620
the total of the tuition money. Sometime later,
the school was apparently closed down completely.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.800
She's inspired others to do good

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.540
Marilyn Mosby, who prosecuted the 2015 case
for the wrongful death of Freddy Gray cut

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.090
her teeth on Judge Judy. Back in 2000, the
then-Tuskegee University student appeared

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.940
before Judge Judy, suing her neighbor for
throwing a baby shower in her apartment, which

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.550
destroyed the residence. That must've been
one wild shower. According to the Daily News,

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:29.460
Mosby handled herself like a pro, bringing
photographic evidence of the destruction with

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.200
her. She ultimately won her case, and from
there, went on to study at Boston College

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:37.210
Law School. The rest is history. Talk about
stepping up in life.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.440
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.430
just saw. And leave us a comment to tell us
what surprised you most about Judge Judy...

